/*
 * mbir_vm.hell — MBIR interpreter in HeLL (Malbolge).
 *
 * MBIR_VERSION = 0, signed-byte model (0..255) carried in Malbolge trits as
 * 0..255 (active low byte; ternary).
 *
 * Architecture:
 *   - stdin: MBIR bytecode length (N bytes as raw input) — actually simpler:
 *     MBIR bytecode supplied via stdin as a byte stream, terminated by EOF.
 *   - Load phase: read stdin byte by byte into a data array CODE[].
 *   - Execution: dispatch on CODE[pc], execute opcode, advance pc.
 *   - Halting: opcode HALT ends execution (stop; not a Malbolge halt unless
 *     encoded as one in the final byte... no: the VM halts the Malbolge
 *     process, equivalent to A_MBIR_HALT).
 *
 * Coverage: PUSH_CONST, POP, DUP, LOAD_LOCAL, STORE_LOCAL,
 *   ADD, SUB, MUL, CMP_EQ, CMP_LT, CMP_GT, JUMP, JUMP_IF_FALSE,
 *   CALL, RETURN, OUT_BYTE, IN_BYTE, HALT.
 */
